{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e19bdc88-8720-4a18-bfda-8b8705671811","agentId":"a0c9a4cf695e65888","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are a mechanistic-interpretability researcher. I am going to show you ONE figure from a paper, with NO surrounding text. Your job is to tell me what you think this figure is claiming, purely from the figure itself (title, axes, legend, bars, lines).\n\nRead this image file: /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win/figures/fig1_final.png\n\nThen answer concisely:\n1. In one sentence, what is the figure claiming? (the takeaway a reader should leave with)\n2. What do the x and y axes mean, and is \"up\" or \"down\" / \"left\" or \"right\" good?\n3. What are the methods being compared, and which one \"wins\"? By roughly how much?\n4. What does the RIGHT panel add over the left panel — what specific objection does it seem designed to pre-empt?\n5. Anything confusing, ambiguous, or unexplained that made you hesitate? (label clarity, undefined terms, missing units, etc.)\n\nBe honest about what is and isn't clear from the figure ALONE. Do not look at any other files — only the image."},"uuid":"9207ffd6-4fa2-493c-a817-2e58e3b10b69","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:33:44.586Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
